  "finalAnswer": "For general medical education, the typical warning signs of a severe allergic reaction (anaphylaxis) affecting breathing and circulation are described below.\n\nThese symptoms can appear quickly and affect multiple body systems. Please note that these are examples of general medical terminology and do not constitute a complete diagnostic list.\n\n### Signs Affecting Breathing\nWhen the airway or breathing is involved, signs may include:\n*   Swelling of the throat or tongue\n*   Feeling like something is stuck in the throat (throat tightness)\n*   Difficulty breathing or shortness of breath\n*   Wheezing\n*   Stridor (a high-pitched, noisy breathing sound)\n\n### Signs Affecting Circulation\nWhen blood pressure or circulation is affected, signs may include:\n*   Weak pulse\n*   Rapid pulse or fast heartbeat\n*   Low blood pressure (hypotension)\n*   Dizziness\n*   Fainting or loss of consciousness\n\n**Important Disclaimer:** If these symptoms occur, emergency medical attention is usually required. This information is for educational purposes only and does not replace professional medical advice or diagnosis.",
